body:
You're returning the size of the wrong buffer. It needs to be the size of the index buffer, not the vertex buffer.

`surface_get_arrays` is also non-trivial to call every time like this, as it allocates/constructs a new array every time, which is why I suggested caching the value.

However, it seems there's a much cheaper way to get the index buffer size, using `Mesh::surface_get_array_index_len`, which would mean we don't have to cache anything.

I haven't actually tried compiling/running this, but something like this should hopefully work:

```suggestion
	int index_count = 0;
	if (mesh->surface_get_format(0) & Mesh::ARRAY_FORMAT_INDEX) {
		index_count = mesh->surface_get_array_index_len(0);
	} else {
		index_count = mesh->surface_get_array_len(0);
	}

	return index_count;
```

